					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-79120#post-4834001</guid>
				<title>SCP-343: My (useless) opinion</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-79120/scp-343#post-4834001</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 02 Dec 2020 02:02:46 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dhanoj</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4381042</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Is this a really bad SCP? Yes. It has potential, but the author didnt do anything with it. Even for a series 1 this is bad. Now, I understand an SCP as old as this one not holding up to our standards and not being changed because of that is fine, but if this was considered a decent SCP back then, im not sure I want to check out the removed SCPs from then.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13892068#post-4833987</guid>
				<title>SCP-5345: </title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13892068/scp-5345#post-4833987</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 02 Dec 2020 01:37:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Calibri Bold</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5045819</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>There's definitely some potential to the premise here, but the execution didn't really pan out well. 5345 just sort of dumps exposition everywhere, and the whole thing feels almost&#8230; meaningless, I want to say. Like nothing really ends up happening, we just learn 5345's backstory and that's about it. 5345 himself is alright, although his character kind of gets stale after a while. Altogether, while I think there's definitely something to tap into here, it just didn't do it for me.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
